    <string name="ob_1_text">Akış shares the videos, music and photos on your phone with TVs, VLC and computers at home. No ads, no account, nothing leaves your network.</string>
    <string name="ob_1_title">Your phone, your media server</string>
    <string name="ob_2_text">Connect the phone and the other device to the same Wi-Fi (the phone\'s hotspot works too), then tap the big button on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="ob_2_title">Same Wi-Fi, one tap</string>
    <string name="ob_3_extra">VLC: Local Network → Universal Plug\'n\'Play\nTV: Source / Media / Home network\nWindows: File Explorer → Network</string>
    <string name="ob_3_text">Your phone shows up as a media server under the name you set.</string>
    <string name="ob_3_title">Find it on the TV and in VLC</string>
    <string name="ob_4_text">Open the address on the home screen (or scan its QR code) in any browser on a computer, TV or another phone. Akış\'s own player, subtitles and file browser are there.</string>
    <string name="ob_4_title">Or just open a browser</string>
    <string name="ob_5_text">Allow access to your media so Akış can list it. You can choose categories and hide folders later in Sources.</string>
    <string name="ob_5_title">What should be shared?</string>
    <string name="ob_6_extra">Remote access (over the internet) is off by default. Turn it on in Settings only if you need it, and read the warnings there.</string>
    <string name="ob_6_text">Anyone on your Wi-Fi can see the server. In Settings you can turn on device approval and a web PIN.</string>
    <string name="ob_6_title">Keep it safe</string>
